From ad23e792959016c9e7b2a371d28b64102ff72bae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Trung=20L=C3=AA?= <8@tle.id.au>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 03:06:01 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 18/25] Generalise the gfx/2d VSX kernels to plain AltiVec for
 the PowerPC 970

The convolution filter, filter-processing SIMD primitives and luminance
mask kernels carried over from the main branch used VSX unaligned loads
and stores, a 64-bit lane splat and the VSX float multiply and divide.
This ESR tree still serves the PowerPC 970 (Apple G5), so the kernels now
use the lvsl/vperm load and rotate plus vec_ste store idioms, 32-bit lane
construction, vmaddfp with a -0.0 addend for the float multiply and a
per-lane divide when VSX is not available, with the VSX forms kept under
__VSX__. They are renamed from VSX to AltiVec, built whenever the target
baseline has AltiVec, and selected at run time through supports_vmx().
